course: dictionary
lesson: 5891
title: Manure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Manure is animal poo, often mixed with straw. Farmers and gardeners spread it on soil because it makes the soil richer, so plants grow better. When you meet a word like this, look at the words around it. «Farmers spread manure and slurry, a runny mix of muck and water, on fields as fertiliser.» The word spread tells you manure is something you put on the ground.
explain: Context can also tell you whether a word is a thing or an action. «In a biogas plant, bacteria break down food waste and manure and make a gas that can be burned for electricity or heat.» Here manure is a thing that the bacteria break down. To manure a field means to spread manure on it, so the word can be a verb too.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Farmers spread animal poo, often mixed with straw, on fields as fertiliser» still makes sense, so your meaning works. If it does not make sense, look again at the clues or use a dictionary.
fact: Manure is animal poo, often mixed with straw.
fact: Manure is a noun, and to manure a field is a verb: you spread manure on it.
fact: Manure makes soil richer so that plants grow better.
fact: Slurry is a runny mix of muck and water.
fact: Green manure means plants dug into the soil to feed it.
exercise: «Farmers spread manure and slurry on fields as fertiliser.» What is manure? | *Animal poo, often mixed with straw | A kind of plant that grows in fields | A machine that cuts grass
exercise: «Farmers spread manure and slurry, a runny mix of muck and water, on fields.» What is slurry? | A type of seed | *A runny mix of muck and water | A thick, sweet syrup | Dry sand used for building
exercise: «In a biogas plant, bacteria break down food waste and manure and make a gas.» What do the bacteria do to the manure? | Freeze it solid | Sell it to shops | *Break it down | Paint it bright colours
test: «The farmer manured the field before planting the seeds.» What does manured mean here? | Cut the grass short for hay | *Spread manure on the field to make the soil richer | Dug a deep hole for a pond
test: «Green manure» means plants dug into the soil to feed it. What is green manure? | *Plants dug into the soil to feed it | Animal poo mixed with straw | A green machine for cutting hedges | Green paint sprayed on fields
exam: «In a biogas plant, bacteria break down food waste and manure to make a gas that can be burned for electricity or heat.» Why can a food waste bin end up making electricity? | Bins are powered by batteries that never run out | Farmers use the bins to hold manure in the fields | Bins have tiny wind turbines inside them | *Bacteria in a biogas plant break the waste down into a gas that can be burned
